---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Architecture" description="How podcast-transcriber works internally, and what is planned next.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-4">Architecture</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-12">How the processing pipeline works internally, the SQLite ledger schema, and what is planned next.</p>

    <!-- 1. Processing Flow -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-6">
        <span class="text-indigo-400 mr-2">1.</span>Processing Flow
      </h2>
      <pre class="bg-gray-900 rounded p-6 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed"><code>RSS feed
  ↓
Episode selection (interactive CLI)
  ↓
Download (skip if hash-verified)
  ↓
Transcribe (base first pass)
  ↓
Score segments (green / yellow / red)
  ↓
Re-transcribe yellow → turbo
  ↓
Re-transcribe red → large-v3  (if --enable-large-pass)
  ↓
Write artifacts (.txt  .srt  .json  .nfo)
  ↓
Update SQLite ledger</code></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. SQLite Ledger -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-6">
        <span class="text-indigo-400 mr-2">2.</span>SQLite State Ledger
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-5">
        Stored at <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">podcasts/.podcast_transcriber_state.sqlite</code>.
        Every episode is a single row identified by <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">(feed_url, episode_guid, audio_sha256, model, language)</code> — processing the same episode with different models creates separate records.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-3">What is tracked per episode</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="text-left border-b border-gray-700">
              <th class="pb-3 pr-6 text-gray-300 font-semibold">Field group</th>
              <th class="pb-3 text-gray-300 font-semibold">Details</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Feed metadata</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">URL, title, slug</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Episode metadata</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">Title, slug, GUID, audio URL, publication date</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Config</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">Model, language, pipeline mode</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Paths</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">Audio, txt, srt, json, nfo</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Step statuses</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">download, transcription, metadata, nfo, overall</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Integrity</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">SHA256 + file size + mtime for all artifacts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Errors</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">Last error message, retry count</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 text-gray-300">Timing</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-400">Started, last updated, completed timestamps</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-3">Step status values</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
        {[
          { status: "pending", desc: "Not started" },
          { status: "running", desc: "In progress" },
          { status: "done", desc: "Completed and verified" },
          { status: "failed", desc: "Error occurred" },
          { status: "partial", desc: "Some steps done" },
          { status: "stale", desc: "Audio changed after transcription" },
        ].map(({ status, desc }) => (
          <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded p-3">
            <code class="text-indigo-400 text-sm">{status}</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">{desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Stale Detection + Crash Recovery -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-6">
        <span class="text-indigo-400 mr-2">3.</span>Stale Detection and Crash Recovery
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-2">Stale detection</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
            Every artifact's SHA256 hash is recorded at write time. On the next run, if the hash of the audio file has changed (e.g. re-downloaded with different encoding), the transcript is automatically marked <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">stale</code> and will be re-transcribed. This prevents silently keeping mismatched transcripts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-2">Crash recovery</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
            At startup, any episode with a <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">running</code> status is automatically reset to <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">partial</code>. This means a process killed mid-transcription will be picked up and retried on the next run — no manual intervention needed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-2">Batch safety</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
            A failure on one episode does not stop the rest of the batch. All errors are recorded in the ledger with the error message and retry count. Use <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">--retry-failed</code> to re-process only the failed episodes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Roadmap -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">
        <span class="text-indigo-400 mr-2">4.</span>Roadmap
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-5">
        The items below are <span class="bg-gray-800 text-yellow-400 text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded">not yet built</span>. The DB schema includes a <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">pipeline_stages</code> table designed to accommodate them.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {[
          { label: "Diarization", desc: "Separate audio into per-speaker segments." },
          { label: "Speaker identification", desc: "Name recurring speakers across episodes." },
          { label: "Chapter extraction", desc: "Detect and label chapter boundaries automatically." },
          { label: "Embeddings + semantic indexing", desc: "Embed transcript segments for search and similarity." },
          { label: "Read-only API over SQLite ledger", desc: "Expose episode state and transcripts via a local HTTP API." },
          { label: "Web UI for reviewing yellow/red segments", desc: "Browser interface for manual review and correction of low-confidence segments." },
          { label: "Summaries", desc: "Automatic episode summarization." },
        ].map(({ label, desc }) => (
          <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4 flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="bg-gray-700 text-yellow-400 text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 shrink-0">planned</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-gray-200 font-medium text-sm">{label}</span>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-0.5">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Repo note -->
    <section class="mb-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-4">
        <span class="text-indigo-400 mr-2">5.</span>Repository Layout
      </h2>
      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5 text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-2">
        <p>
          This documentation website lives inside the same repository as the CLI under <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">web/</code>.
          That co-location is intentional for now — it keeps docs and code in sync.
        </p>
        <p>
          A future split into separate packages (<code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">podcast-transcriber-core</code>, <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">api</code>, <code class="bg-gray-900 px-1 rounded text-xs">web</code>) is possible once the API and web layers are built out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Layout>
